  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppRC 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'Months after a new treatment is approved, some patients are asked to
    complete follow-up surveys so researchers can learn how the treatment is working
    over time.


    <b>Once a new treatment is approved for widespread use, research
    coordinators must analyze follow-up data and decide what the results mean for
    patient care.<b>


    Is this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?'
  explanation: Research coordinators help coordinate follow-up and ensure information
    is collected and shared accurately, but they do not analyze the data or make
    decisions about patient care. By carefully organizing patient surveys and reports,
    they help ensure real-world experiences are clearly documented so experts can
    review them and take action if needed.
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Approval
